 "method": "No code could be executed, so this is a hand-constructed representative sample, not a true random Monte Carlo draw. Process fractions were estimated from NIST water attenuation data at 1.17/1.33 MeV: Compton about 99%, pair about 0.5%, Rayleigh about 0.2%, photoelectric negligible. Primary/scattered split was taken as about 70/30 at 5 cm depth for a 10x10 field. Primary Compton angles were sampled from Klein-Nishina weights in discrete bins. Outgoing photon and electron energies came from Compton kinematics, and electron angles from tan(phi) = cot(theta/2)/(1+alpha). Scattered photons were taken at 0.2-0.7 MeV. Pair kinetic energies share 1.3325 - 1.022 MeV.",
